# Synthetic Data Generation with GANs for Manufacturing

A conditional WGAN-GP architecture for generating synthetic sensor and process data in manufacturing scenarios with limited historical data. This system enabled model training with 70% less historical data while maintaining performance.

## Architecture

![GAN Architecture](docs/gan_architecture.png)

The system uses a Wasserstein GAN with gradient penalty (WGAN-GP) approach, enhanced with physics-informed constraints and conditional generation capabilities to produce realistic manufacturing data.

## Key Features
- Conditional generation based on process parameters
- Physics-informed constraints to ensure realistic values
- Progressive growing architecture for training stability
- Automated quality filtering to reject unrealistic samples
- Statistical validation framework for synthetic data

## Results
The system generates synthetic manufacturing data that matches the statistical distribution of real data with a Jensen-Shannon divergence of only 0.032. Models trained on the synthetic data maintain 97% of the performance of models trained on complete historical datasets.

